10:                             spliced in -- object removal, background swap)
11:   C. FACE-SWAP             (real video/photo, a different face composited
12:                             in -- classic "deepfake", reenactment)
13: 
14: Architecture: rather than one global score, this runs THREE independent
15: forensic families (see forensics_core.py) and reports a verdict PLUS the
16: ranked list of findings that drove it -- "fake because X, in region Y" --
17: not just a number. If nothing fires, it says so plainly instead of forcing
18: a guess.
19: 
20: Combination logic:
21:   - Each family (global / splice / per-face) produces its own sub-score.
22:   - The OVERALL verdict is FAKE if *any* family crosses its threshold --
23:     a photo can be 95% real and have one small AI-inpainted region; a
24:     global average would wash that out, so we deliberately do NOT average
25:     across families. We take the max, with the global pretrained-model
26:     signal as an independent strong vote.
27:   - The "reason" is the full list of individual findings that crossed
28:     their own threshold, sorted by score.
29: 
30: Setup:
31:   pip install torch transformers pillow opencv-python-headless numpy retina-face --break-system-packages
32: """
